[('Medicines and daily habits','Treatment usually starts with appropriate medicines and practical changes to eating and daily habits.'),('Tests before considering surgery','Endoscopy, reflux testing or tests of food-pipe movement may be advised to establish the cause and guide the operation.'),('An individual surgical plan','Persistent symptoms or selected hernias may lead to a discussion about repair and fundoplication. The choice depends on the findings.')],
